<pdd-reason>The author's private tracking view. A pitch is invisible to everyone else until it clears screening, so without this dialog the act of pitching ends in silence — and silence reads as the idea being thrown away.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"MyPitchesModal","signature":"function MyPitchesModal(props: MyPitchesModalProps): JSX.Element | null","returns":"the author-only dialog; null when open is false"},
  {"name":"MyPitchesModalProps","signature":"type MyPitchesModalProps = { open: boolean; onClose: () => void; pending: PendingPitch[]; features: Feature[]; loading?: boolean; error?: string | null; onDismiss: (feature_id: string) => void; onRetry?: () => void }","returns":"the component contract"}
]}}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>prompts/frontend/api_client_typescript.prompt</pdd-dependency>

Implement `frontend/src/components/my_pitches_modal.tsx`. `PendingPitch` and `Feature` are imported
as types from `../api_client`; there is no `contracts.ts`. The shell calls
`api_client.getMyPitches` and passes both lists down.

<responsibility>
Show one author every pitch they have made — still screening, dropped, merged, or live — in a single private dialog.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
This module DOES NOT fetch; the shell owns the read and passes both lists in, so this dialog unit-tests without a network.
This module DOES NOT render anywhere near the public feed. These entries are unverified content and putting them inline with the board is the exact failure screening exists to prevent.
This module DOES NOT let the author edit, retract, or re-submit a pitch — the pipeline owns a pitch once it is queued.
This module DOES NOT import `styles.css`; the shell imports it once for the whole app.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
**Pending** — a pitch that exists only in Redis under a TTL: still `screening`, or terminally `rejected` or `merged`. It has a `feature_id` but no Postgres row, and it disappears on its own when the TTL lapses.
**Merged** — not a rejection. The author's idea joined an existing feature and their vote went with it; the copy celebrates rather than apologises.
Duplicate: a pitch the PM agent judged to be the same idea as an existing feature. It is merged into that feature rather than dropped, which is why its outcome is `merged` and not `rejected`.
**Invisible rejection** — the public board never shows that a pitch was dropped. This dialog is the only place the author learns it, and only the author sees it.
</vocabulary>

<capabilities>
- MAY sort and group the lists it is handed.
- MUST NOT call `fetch`, `api_client`, or Supabase.
- MUST NOT add a hex value, font, radius, or animation — compose only `modal-backdrop`, `modal`, `modal-head`, `modal-close`, `modal-hint`, `pitches-list`, `pitches-empty`, `pending-card`, `is-rejected`, `pending-copy`, `pending-status`, `shield`, `btn-ghost`, `btn-dismiss`, `pill` and its stage variants.
</capabilities>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Render the dialog titled `My pitches` with the hint `🔒 Only you can see these. A pitch joins the public feed once Guardagent clears it.` The lock is the point: an author needs to know this view is theirs alone before it shows them a rejection.
R2 (MUST): Show `pending` above `features`, each sorted newest first. An author cares most about what is still unresolved.
R3 (MUST): Render a `screening` entry with the pulsing `shield` and `🛡️ Guardagent is screening your pitch...`, and no dismiss control — there is nothing to dismiss yet.
R4 (MUST): Map every rejection `reason` to its own line and never fall back to a generic message: `security` → "Your pitch didn't clear screening — rephrase and try again."; `off_topic` → "Great idea, but it's outside what this app is about — check the Sandbox to see what we're building."; `unclear` → "Your title and description seemed to describe different things — try again with them lined up."; `already_shipped` → "Looks like this already shipped in {shipped_version} — check it out in the Sandbox!" A generic "rejected" teaches the author nothing and guarantees they pitch the same thing again.
R5 (MUST NOT): Show the screener's raw verdict, model output, confidence, or internal detail. The author gets the actionable sentence, not the machine's reasoning.
R6 (MUST): Render a `merged` entry as a win — `🔗 Great minds! Your idea joined forces with "{merged_into_title}"` — visually distinct from a rejection, and MUST NOT mark it `is-rejected`. Losing a duplicate to a stronger feature is the system working, and dressing it as a failure punishes the behaviour the product wants.
R7 (MUST): Give `rejected` and `merged` entries a Dismiss control calling `onDismiss` with the entry's `feature_id`. A terminal entry the author cannot clear turns the tray into a list of old disappointments.
R8 (MUST): Render each of the author's existing `features` as one compact read-only row — title, current stage pill, and `upvotes` — with no vote button and no click-through action. The public board is where an author interacts with a live feature; this is a status list.
R9 (MUST): Render a friendly empty state inviting a first pitch when both lists are empty, using `pitches-empty`.
R10 (MUST): Render distinct loading and error states, showing the error message with a retry control when `onRetry` is supplied. An empty tray and an unreachable server are opposite facts, and showing the first when the second is true tells the author their pitch vanished.
R11 (MUST): Use `role="dialog"` with `aria-modal="true"`, labelled by its own heading, and close on the ✕ control, on backdrop click, and on `Escape`.
R12 (MUST): Move focus into the dialog on open and return it to the opener on close.
R13 (MUST NOT): Render `feature_id` or any other id as visible text. It is passed to `onDismiss`, never printed.
R14 (MUST): Treat an entry that has disappeared between reads as dismissed rather than as an error — `rejected` and `merged` entries lapse with their 72-hour TTL, and a pitch that clears screening is removed when its Realtime insert arrives.
</contract_rules>

<pdd>
This dialog is the whole of US-06's UI. It replaces the inline pending tray an earlier draft of the
shell rendered above the feed — that put unscreened titles one CSS mistake away from the public
board, and the mock's masthead-button-plus-dialog is both safer and less cluttered.

`merged` is deliberately a peer of `rejected` in `PendingPitch.state` rather than a rejection
reason. The two outcomes differ in what the author should feel and in whether a public row exists
to point at, and collapsing them would lose both distinctions.

Promotion out of this dialog is driven by the shell: when the Realtime insert for a pending
`feature_id` arrives, the shell drops the entry and celebrates. That never fires for a `merged`
entry, whose `feature_id` never becomes a row — which is why R6's copy has to carry the outcome
itself.
</pdd>

